# Pinned revision of the external Ceph s3-tests suite.
#
# WHY A COMMIT AND NOT A TAG
#   ceph/s3-tests has never published a tag or a release: `git ls-remote --tags` returns
#   nothing at all. Tracking `master` would mean two consecutive weekly runs are not
#   comparable, and the ratchet in ci/s3tests/xfail.txt would ratchet against noise.
#
# HOW THIS PIN WAS VERIFIED (2026-09-02)
#   git ls-remote https://github.com/ceph/s3-tests master
#     -> 5522d1c351f75bc00ae0f64f742f3f095f5939d9  refs/heads/master
#   git ls-remote --tags https://github.com/ceph/s3-tests
#     -> (no output)
#   gh api repos/ceph/s3-tests --jq .license.spdx_id
#     -> MIT
#
# HOW TO MOVE IT
#   Raise the SHA in its own pull request, re-run the workflow in `record` mode, and land
#   the resulting xfail list separately. Moving the pin and the tolerated set in one commit
#   makes it impossible to tell an upstream change from a behaviour change.
#
# Sourced by ci/s3tests/run.sh and by .github/workflows/e2e-s3tests.yml.
S3TESTS_REPOSITORY=https://github.com/ceph/s3-tests
S3TESTS_SHA=5522d1c351f75bc00ae0f64f742f3f095f5939d9
S3TESTS_PYTHON=3.12
